{"id":"Q04","kind":"qa","request":{"mode":"question","attempt_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014","question":"For the section 6.1 exemption concerning a newly built building or an addition, what occupancy and existing-tenancy limits apply, and who must prove the exemption in a dispute? Is the current tenant moving in after 2018 enough by itself?"},"letter":null,"expected_extract":null,"expected_status":"answered","expected_tool":null,"expected_tool_args":null,"expected_tool_result":null,"required_claims":[{"id":"c1","text":"For the building-or-addition exemption, no part of the relevant building or addition may have been occupied for residential purposes on or before November 15, 2018."},{"id":"c2","text":"A current tenant moving in after November 15, 2018 does not by itself establish the building-or-addition exemption."},{"id":"c3","text":"The exemption does not apply to the protected tenancy under an agreement entered into on or before November 15, 2018; that protection does not extend to subsequent tenancies."},{"id":"c4","text":"The landlord bears the burden of proving the section 6.1 exemption when it is disputed before the Board."}],"evidence_ids":["76e43ee03b23a15cb3a289c5a3da5f0289ecfdd030e8e387ffb980bb4eec7c16","c97c40201489f9b11e5d36c78e2873e2a37f92954804d7a56c6c4245dd135f3e","cd3315e72a9ca27705d2ab881c15481f5cd52ea2febb3320f82f0c1e57fbbde8"],"relevance":{"24f67b51a6bb8c7ee92df4526f550c536fb477235a8ae893c19efdc926da52d2":1,"76e43ee03b23a15cb3a289c5a3da5f0289ecfdd030e8e387ffb980bb4eec7c16":2,"7caca7076be4934b4f4a8a29cc341ee9f12d2b26bf2bfa778e754fe660df5256":1,"b0e650241164fd4a77ae93377f48b2b049494a5f55616d3b6f9ee8897fb1268b":1,"c46d0af95c657c29d63e6ac979d2308905efd045383c19f1da705cb18fce024d":1,"c97c40201489f9b11e5d36c78e2873e2a37f92954804d7a56c6c4245dd135f3e":2,"cd3315e72a9ca27705d2ab881c15481f5cd52ea2febb3320f82f0c1e57fbbde8":2}}
